The VES survey at Choba-LawnTennisField identifies a five-layer subsurface profile. The resistivity starts at 91.2 ohm-m, increases to 380.2 ohm-m in the second layer, and then drops significantly to 43.25 ohm-m in the third layer. The sequence then trends upward through the fourth layer (474.3 ohm-m) and the fifth layer (597.1 ohm-m). 

Applying the curve-type notation rules: the first group (91.2, 380.2, 43.25) is K, the second group (380.2, 43.25, 474.3) is H, and the third group (43.25, 474.3, 597.1) is A. This results in a KHA-type curve, which is consistent with the classification currently on file.

